@focus id=ACTIVE-001 c=H :: bounded main-roadmap Milestone6 complete+commit-ready; M7 now owns 7.1 reproducible Yosys/ABC jobs,7.2 linked modules/libraries+bounded elaboration,7.3 reset-enable/NBA expansion+simulation-only initial policy,7.4 persisted synthesis results+cross-probing; README is user-oriented with RTL limits+release/arm64 DMG builds.
@handoff id=HANDOFF-001 c=H :: state=bounded M6 commit-ready; new .ochippy saves persist circuit+physical cache and reopen 3D without placement/routing rebuild when digest/version match; legacy .chippy opens; next=commit then M7 synthesis boundary; physical stray-geometry audit retained; val=rust121+web+tauri-release
@fact id=PRODUCT-001 c=H :: OpenChippy=education-first desktop VLSI studio; Rust owns authoritative models/services; React/Three.js own interaction and visualization.
@constraint id=CONSTRAINT-001 c=H :: preserve user changes; source of truth=code; avoid later-milestone expansion without user scope.
@dec id=ARCH-OWNERSHIP-001 c=H :: serializable project/history/simulation/DRC remain UI-independent Rust; Tauri commands are thin adapters; view state is ephemeral frontend state.
@dec id=M6-RTL-BOUNDARY-001 c=H :: OpenChippy owns a small deterministic scalar structural-Verilog IR/parser; one module,ANSI/classic ports,wires,primitive positional instances,and simple assign/~assign accepted; unsupported behavioral/broad HDL synthesis remains explicit and is deferred to Yosys integration in M7.
@dec id=M6-INCHSTONES-001 c=H :: order=6.1 structural IR/parser API,6.2 nonmutating file preview+diagnostics,6.3 logical project mapping,6.4 stable export+parse roundtrip,6.5 gate-level hierarchy viewer+cross-probing.
@dec id=PROJECT-LIFECYCLE-001 c=H :: New/Open reset history boundary; Rust workspace owns path,saved snapshot,dirty,undo,redo; circuit rename is persisted+undoable.
@dec id=SCHEMATIC-001 c=H :: CMOS transistors primary; wires persist terminal refs plus optional free endpoint+ordered waypoints; junction=node; output=in; net_label=node.
@dec id=SCHEMATIC-BLOCK-GEOM-001 c=H :: reusable symbol height derives max(input,output) pin bank; width derives name+max(power,ground); edge pins fan at .72 units with .36 gap; Rust terminal_position and SVG renderer use identical geometry; selection bounds are symbol-specific.
@dec id=NAV-001 c=H :: schematic wheel/trackpad pans; pinch or modifier-wheel zooms; empty drag/arrows pan; Shift-click multi-select; 3D uses MapControls.
@dec id=DRC-001 c=H :: Rust graph DRC has stable codes; equal-name labels join nets; dangling wire is warning; checks floating,shorted rails,duplicates,disconnected,missing power.
@dec id=LAYOUT-001 c=H :: 3D targets Magic/PDK-style inferred cell layout in abstract technology units; schematic junctions are not physical vias.
@dec id=ROUTER-001 c=H :: Rust preview reserves a size-aware central signal channel; each net has unique Y track; top available metal carries horizontal trunks; process permitting,power/PMOS/NMOS long drops use distinct lower directional layers; transitions add intermediate landing metals+adjacent vias; tracks do not traverse device banks/rails; max-layer bound and NAND cross-net overlap tests enforced.
@dec id=ROUTER-PITCH-001 c=H :: channel track pitch=landing 0.28+clearance 0.04=0.32; via=0.24; pin landing height=0.28; transistor X/Y pitch unchanged; regression requires compact pitch and same-layer isolation.
@dec id=CAMERA-001 c=H :: orthographic top view fits post-generation physical bounds; normalized frustum+zoom keeps center stable; Top view resets.
@dec id=SIM-MODEL-001 c=H :: NMOS conducts iff gate HIGH; PMOS iff gate LOW; outputs={HIGH,LOW,FLOATING,CONTENDED,UNKNOWN}; unknown gates conservatively propagate uncertainty without degrading driven rails.
@dec id=SIM-SETTLE-001 c=H :: switch_state treats provisional FLOATING gate as open so upstream combinational hierarchy can settle without UNKNOWN poisoning of rail-connected groups; explicit UNKNOWN/CONTENDED gates remain SwitchState::Unknown and propagate uncertainty.
@dec id=SIM-API-001 c=H :: backend returns net/output/transistor/wire states; frontend never reimplements solver; palette HIGH=green LOW=blue FLOATING=gray CONTENDED=red UNKNOWN=amber.
@dec id=TRUTH-001 c=H :: truth tables enumerate inputs in component order via production solver, preserve five states+convergence, cap at 8 inputs, and rows can drive live visualization.
@dec id=WAVE-001 c=H :: waveform time unit=integer ns; CLK/CLOCK inputs toggle at half-period; others form binary sequence at change interval; sample only event boundaries.
@dec id=M4-WAVE-BUS-001 c=H :: Project owns validated WaveformGroup{id,name,signals MSB->LSB,radix,collapsed}; one scalar belongs to max one bus; rename/delete maintain refs; UI derives aggregate intervals after resolving all same-time samples; unknown/floating/contended=>X; stable labels+cursor/edge share formatter; crossed X boundary on value change; expand preserves scalar data.
@dec id=M4-WAVE-ZOOM-001 c=H :: waveform time axis zoom=1x..32x via Fit/-/+ or Ctrl/Cmd-wheel; scaling preserves viewport center, increases tick count proportionally,and uses zoomed interval pixel width to reveal aggregate values inside traces.
@dec id=M4-WAVE-INTERVAL-001 c=H :: aggregate interval builder merges adjacent member-event slices with identical formatted bus value before width/label decisions; prevents dense no-op input samples suppressing readable trace values.
@dec id=WAVE-BOUNDS-001 c=H :: duration<=1,000,000ns; transitions<=10,000; duration affects time mapping not SVG size; lanes fixed at 52px.
@dec id=M3-PLAN-001 c=H :: M3 slices isolate technology schema,file I/O,device geometry,threshold/resistance behavior,then capacitance/delay; every slice preserves prior truth tables or adds monotonicity tests.
@dec id=M3-TECHFILE-001 c=H :: technology YAML format=1 uses technology header plus nmos/pmos blocks; max_metal_layers is required in YAML,min=2,EDU=5; older embedded JSON defaults=5; concise vt/ron/reference aliases accepted; unknown/missing/nonphysical fields rejected; validated snapshot embedded in Project.
@dec id=M3-GEOMETRY-001 c=H :: Component has optional deviceGeometry W/L; new MOS use active-tech reference values; missing old data resolves to polarity-specific reference; Ron=RonNom*(L/Lref)*(Wref/W), Cgate=CgatePerW*W*(L/Lref), Cdiff=CdiffPerW*W; Rust is authoritative.
@dec id=M3-TIMING-001 c=H :: net load sums connected MOS gate and drain/source diffusion capacitance; resolved high/low uses corresponding active path R; delay_ns=0.69*Rohm*Cff*1e-6; waveform output transitions retain fractional ns while static truth tables remain operating-point results.
@dec id=M3-DRIVE-001 c=H :: static solver maps HIGH=technology VDD,LOW=0; NMOS selected HIGH conducts only VDD>Vtn, PMOS selected LOW conducts only VDD>|Vtp|; unknown gates remain unknown; active weighted graph reports shortest high/low drive path resistance by summing device Ron.
@dec id=M3-PHYS-001 c=H :: M3.6 physical synthesis uses Rust layout IR independent of schematic coordinates; normalize topology,share diffusion,place rows,route layers,check rules+connectivity,then derive identical 2D/GDS and 3D geometry.
@dec id=M3-PHYS-IR-001 c=H :: physical IR v1 contains technology/source identity,sorted MOS devices with W/L+gate/drain/source net IDs,canonical nets with roles+terminals,and sorted external pins; schematic positions,rotations,wire routes absent; Tauri generate_physical_ir is read-only.
@dec id=M3-PHYS-PREVIEW-001 c=H :: Rust compact_preview emits generic base/process-bounded metal+via layer strings with fixed rows/rails+connectivity anchors; M1 carries power/device drops,signals cycle across M2..configured max,and transitions receive landing metal+via stacks; PHVIEW builds matching layer styles/toggles dynamically; router remains provisional.
@dec id=M3-PHYS-FOLD-001 c=H :: compact_preview scores candidate column counts by aspect-ratio error,folds each polarity into multiple banks,expands rails/well/substrate to footprint,and staggers row drops; 128-MOS regression requires aspect<1.5; topology/hierarchy-aware macro floorplanning remains next.
@dec id=M3-NAV-SCALE-001 c=H :: schematic zoom width=2..4096,F/Home fits placed components+wire geometry,Shift-arrows accelerate pan; 3D orthographic controls zoom=.00001..200 and Top view/Fit restores IR bounds.
@dec id=SCHEMATIC-OPEN-FIT-001 c=H :: app increments fitRevision only on initial create,New,and Open; schematic fits component+free-wire geometry on revision/mount; ordinary edit/history/simulation workspace replacements preserve camera.
@dec id=WAVE-SCROLL-001 c=H :: waveform root/canvas are height-constrained+overflow-hidden; settings owns vertical scroll; lane grid uses flex-height zero base,explicit vertical scrollbar+independent horizontal time scroll,sticky labels remain synchronized.
@dec id=WAVE-CURSOR-001 c=H :: pointer click/drag maps SVG X to fractional ns; vertical cursor spans all lanes; header reports cursor time; sticky label shows five-state cursor value; horizontal scroll maps left plot boundary to edgeTime; each label owns sticky 1/0/X badge positioned at HIGH/LOW/mid Y for value where trace meets block.
@dec id=M11-SIGNAL-VIZ-001 c=H :: after physical connectivity equivalence,3D shapes retain stable simulation-net identity and can toggle process colors vs HIGH/LOW/FLOATING/CONTENDED/UNKNOWN state; active MOS channels+rail paths highlight; net isolation+waveform cursor update materials without layout regeneration.
@dec id=M4-PHYS-DRC-001 c=H :: versioned process YAML owns units+grid,width,spacing,via/contact size+pitch+enclosure,poly/diffusion,well,metal-area/notch/EOL,tap/rail/pin-access rules; headless Rust checks canonical physical shapes; diagnostics carry stable rule ID,severity,shape IDs,measured/required/layer; 3D overlays select+frame violations; step toward signoff-ready generation,foundry correlation remains M9.
@dec id=PHYS-CANVAS-001 c=H :: defect_plan is controlling closure sequence; PhysicalCanvas is authoritative layer occupancy with rule-derived half-spacing halos+uniform-grid index+owner/net/obstruction metadata; same-net continuous metal may merge but cuts never bypass spacing; illegal route candidates are scored without commit.
@dec id=PHYS-BUILD-010 c=H :: Phases9+10 combined: every emitted DRC diagnostic has category+pipeline origin and aggregate maps; async inspect snapshots project under lock then releases it before spawn_blocking synthesis/DRC; 3D opens immediately with build overlay and persistent retryable failure state; live fine-grained callbacks remain future API.
@dec id=RTL-IMPORT-062 c=H :: Import RTL selects .v/.sv, previews editable source, parses without project mutation, summarizes typed IR, and explicitly diagnoses vectors/parameters/named connections/multi-module input; Accept preview is a deliberate boundary only, with model mutation deferred to 6.3.
@dec id=RTL-MAP-063 c=H :: accepted scalar module persists as separate undoable RtlDesign with unchanged names/connections and deterministic driver-topology levels/coordinates; never fabricate transistor components or physical cells; legacy files default none; packed-vector slice 6.3.1 precedes export.
@dec id=RTL-VECTOR-0631 c=H :: preserve fixed packed range metadata+declared order on ports/nets; primitive connections remain scalar via constant bit selects; reject whole-bus scalar-pin use, out-of-range bits, and part selects distinctly; defer concatenation/signed/multidimensional/parameter-derived widths.
@dec id=RTL-PARAM-0632 c=H :: parameter support is its own pre-export slice: integer defaults+named/positional overrides+bounded constant expressions+effective elaboration before widths; preserve intent; reject unknown/duplicate/cyclic/invalid values; defer generate/defparam/full SV types.
@dec id=RTL-PARAM-IMPL-0632 c=H :: ordered integer defaults evaluate +,-,*,/,unary-,parentheses,earlier params; persist default/override expression+value; generic cells preserve named/positional overrides, primitives reject them; validate external override names/child widths only after library definition linking in 6.5.
@dec id=RTL-EXPORT-064 c=H :: Rust exporter is deterministic/read-only ANSI structural HDL; preserve original parameter/range expressions, directions, nets, primitive+generic instances, override style, constants, bit selects; escape nonstandard names; require parse-export-parse IR equality; defer external definition bundles/transistor-block semantic translation to linking.
@dec id=RTL-ASSIGN-064A c=H :: accept ANSI wire/logic/reg+signedness; preserve nontrivial continuous expressions as assignment IR(target,source text,ordered refs) and export verbatim-deterministically; do not fabricate arithmetic gate networks before synthesis; product UI never mentions internal milestone numbering.
@dec id=RTL-VIEW-065 c=H :: dedicated RTL workspace renders persisted ports,cells,continuous assignments+orthogonal nets; selection inspects source identity/connections/parameters; drag-pan,wheel zoom,fit are view-local; unresolved external cells appear as hierarchy references until linked multi-module/library definitions enable descent.
@dec id=RTL-IMPORT-NAV-065 c=H :: accepting valid RTL must verify returned project.rtlDesign then navigate directly to RTL View; logical-only import must not appear as an unchanged schematic no-op; backend/history remains mutation authority; val=web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-PROC-066 c=H :: procedural support sequence=combinational statement/expression AST+always@*/always_comb+blocking=/definite assignment,then edge-triggered register state+nonblocking scheduling,then simulation-only initial subset; never accept syntax without matching scheduling/hardware semantics.
@dec id=RTL-SIM-0652 c=H :: simulate_waveform selects imported RtlDesign when present; scalarize packed port bits into existing lanes/groups; Rust settles primitives+bounded +,-,&,|,^,~ continuous expressions; clock names use clock period; unsupported/unknown stays UNKNOWN; val=rust109+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-GROUP-0652 c=H :: Project waveform-group validation admits schematic IO names plus scalarized imported RTL port bits; exclusivity/order/persistence rules unchanged; fixes UI picker/backend namespace mismatch; val=rust111+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-COMB-0661 c=H :: always_comb and always @*/@(*) accept ordered blocking assignments with optional begin/end; lower into assignment IR for view,continuous-form export,waveform simulation; bounded if/else+case semantics in dedicated records; <= reserved for stateful 6.6.2.
@dec id=RTL-COMB-IF-0661 c=H :: bounded if/else requires exactly1 blocking assignment per branch+same target; lowers to cond?true:false mux expression; no else=>inferred-latch diagnostic; nested/multi-statement branches deferred; evaluator propagates UNKNOWN condition and selects known branch otherwise; val=rust113+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-TRUTH-0653 c=H :: generate_truth_table selects imported RtlDesign when present; scalarizes packed IO in declared MSB->LSB order; max8 input bits; every row uses same Rust combinational evaluator; unknown output=>nonconverged; transistor path unchanged; val=rust115+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-CASE-0661 c=H :: bounded case requires >=1 value item+exactly1 default+same target all arms; supports sized binary labels; lowers to ordered equality ternary mux chain; missing default=>inferred-latch diagnostic; nested/multi-assignment arms deferred; val=rust115+web+tauri-release.
@constraint id=RTL-CLOSEOUT-066 c=H :: Milestone6 cannot close until clocked always/always_ff nonblocking <= has event/register semantics and a waveform regression proving registered edge transitions; syntax-only acceptance is insufficient.
@dec id=RTL-SEQ-0662 c=H :: RtlModule persists sequentialProcesses(edge,clock,target,expression,refs); always_ff+classic edge always accept exactly1 <= assignment; export preserves edge/NBA+logic output; waveform state starts UNKNOWN, detects edge,evaluates pre-edge,commits all updates together,re-settles combinational; truth table rejects stateful design; RTL View renders register node+clock/data edges; val=rust117+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=RTL-EXPR-06621 c=H :: tokenizer handles quoted strings+{}; (*...*) attributes including quoted/escaped values are consumed as nonsemantic synthesis metadata and disambiguated from @(*); assignment expressions preserve+evaluate concat and constant/parameter replication up to128b; invalid repeat=>UNKNOWN; localparam,shift,unpacked memory,string-param semantics remain explicit follow-up; val=rust119+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=M6-UI-CLOSEOUT-001 c=H :: schematic library+inspector render only in schematic workspace; focused views reclaim full shell width; PHVIEW preserves camera across selection/layer scene rebuilds and exposes lower-right Top/Iso/Front/Right/Fit controls; RTLVIEW computes logical bounds and centers/fits on open+resize; initial+broader reset/enable+linked definition descent deferred explicitly; val=rust119+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=M6-PROJECT-PACKAGE-001 c=H :: default save=.ochippy v1 manifest with includedFiles roles circuit+physical; siblings=<stem>.chippy and <stem>.chippy_gds v1; physical artifact owns deserializable PhysicalLayoutIr v2+stable FNV1a source-project digest; open supports .chippy/.ochippy; valid cache skips normalize_project but recomputes DRC; stale/version/path-escape rejected; standalone physical export available; val=rust121+web+tauri-release.
@dec id=M7-RTL-SYNTH-001 c=H :: deferred M6 RTL is unified with synthesis: 7.1 tool jobs,7.2 multi-module/library linking+child param/width checks+localparam/part-select/shift/bounded memory,7.3 reset-enable+multi-NBA+initial target policy,7.4 netlist metrics+cross-probe; never build parallel importer-only linker.
@dec id=PHYS-CANVAS-TRACKS-001 c=H :: occupancy interval stores dominant H/V orientation and every manufacturing-grid track crossed by perpendicular geometry span; secondary index key=(layer,orientation,track); spatial index remains authority for 2D collision; removal atomically rebuilds both.
@dec id=PHYS-DEVICE-RESERVE-001 c=H :: one grid-snapped device_footprint generator feeds both placement reservation and final IR; diffusion+poly+two contacts commit atomically; illegal nominal sites retry deterministic nearest in-row sites and never emit partial geometry.
@dec id=PHYS-ROUTE-API-001 c=H :: all detailed+render-preview metal/via admission uses PhysicalCanvas.commit_routing_geometry; atomic batches cannot partially mutate occupancy; rejected shapes never enter corresponding IR and collision net ownership drives bounded repair.
@dec id=PHYS-ROUTE-SEED-001 c=H :: every detailed rebuild commits all selected device footprints as one atomic seed transaction before priority-ordered routes; preview commits fixed device shapes before ordered power/signal metal; single route-shape commit avoids full-canvas clone while multi-shape batches remain atomic.
@dec id=PHYS-SPATIAL-DRC-001 c=H :: PhysicalCanvas uniform-grid index has explicit unchecked insertion for already-generated illegal IR; DRC uses indexed same-layer candidate neighbors then exact Euclidean measurement; query_point supplies hit-test primitive; legality commit semantics remain separate.
@dec id=PHYS-INCREMENTAL-ROUTE-001 c=H :: per segment search budget=planned track+±1/±2 then nominal track on compatible alternate layers(max9 in EDU5M); Phase7 index preflights; connectors+landings+full transitions commit with transactional rollback; preview metals precede cuts and unenclosed cuts are removed.
@dec id=PHYS-FROZEN-BLOCK-001 c=H :: hierarchy-aware physical entry emits immutable per-instance implementation IR with owned devices/private nets/shapes,bounds,promoted boundary pins,local DRC; private nets removed from top global plan; internal leaf realization retained only inside macro until definition-level cache reuse.
@open id=VIA-CLEANUP-001 c=H :: zero metal DRC observed but via spacing/orphans remained pre-P6; P6 prevents partial detail transitions+filters unenclosed preview cuts; spacing checker is via-via and same-net cuts obey pitch; still audit redundant same-net arrays/legacy preview fragments.
@dec id=M4-DRC-VIEW-001 c=H :: 3D IR+physical DRC generated together; stable shape indices drive exact emissive highlight; selecting isolates diagnostic layer+frames geometry; filters=rule,severity,layer,derived-net; saved JSON bundles identities,IR version,selected planning/placement,global/detail routing metrics,report.
@dec id=M4-DRC-CLOSURE-001 c=H :: 4.7.1 precedes waveform buses; pairwise spacing fragments coalesce by rule+layer+electrical-net-pair but remain errors; multi-net folded fixture required; access tracks repaired from conflict graph; detailed polygons render/export only after connectivity+DRC closure.
@dec id=M4-VERTICAL-001 c=H :: rejected: net-ID M2/M4 distribution passed synthetic fixture but regressed 4B_ADDER 496->520; reverted to prior bank-separated drops; future layer/track moves require actual conflict-graph score.
@dec id=M4-EMITTED-MPASS-001 c=H :: full IR proved detailed guide polygons lack legal terminal access; direct cutover regressed exact 4B to440 and was rejected; emitted route now evaluates legal connected drop/via layers against unique conflicting nets across original,reverse,high-fanout orders and selects lowest physical spacing score=132; detailed cutover waits connectivity+zeroDRC.
@dec id=M4-CUT-SPACING-001 c=H :: same-net continuous layers merge and skip spacing; contact/via cuts remain discrete and enforce process pitch regardless of net; exact duplicate generated vias dedupe before DRC; cut violations use CUT.MIN_SPACING and coalesce by rule+layer+net pair.
@dec id=M4-ROUTED-SELECT-001 c=H :: every feasible bounded floorplan is placed+global-routed+detailed-routed before selection; rank lexicographically global overflow,detail conflicts,placement score; never commit planning-only square winner when topology plan routes better.
@dec id=M4-INCHSTONES-001 c=H :: order=4.1 rules,4.2 headless DRC,4.3 planning/resources,4.4 placement+legalization,4.5 negotiated global route,4.6 detailed repair+compaction,4.7 3D DRC,4.8 waveform buses.
@dec id=M4-RULEDECK-001 c=H :: Technology embeds defaulted PhysicalRuleDeck v1:DBU/um,manufacturing grid,base diffusion/poly/well/metal width+spacing+area,contact/via size+spacing+enclosure,gate extension,well enclosure,BTree metalN+adjacent viaNN overrides; validation rejects version/nonpositive/off-grid/out-of-range/nonadjacent; old JSON/YAML receive EDU deck; inspector shows version/grid/contact/via.
@dec id=M4-MULTIPASS-001 c=H :: staged deterministic P&R; process tracks/capacity first; 3 placement/aspect candidates; global/high-fanout weighting; capacity-charged guides; negotiated history costs+selective ripup; detailed pin access/track assignment/local repair; rank equivalence>DRC>overflow>area>routing>aspect.
@dec id=M4-BUDGET-001 c=H :: configurable EDU defaults=density 60-70%,estimated route utilization<=75%,3 growth passes of 5-10% congested dimension,30 global iterations+3-stall stop,10 detailed repair rounds; retain best snapshot+report bounded failure.
@dec id=M4-PLAN-001 c=H :: Technology PhysicalPlanningRules owns site/row,density/utilization,growth/iteration budgets,and metal pitch/offset/direction/capacity/power reservation; resolver backfills old tech to metal ceiling; PhysicalPlanningReport owns priority net classes,3 floorplan candidates,selected index,and coarse per-layer capacity bins; compact preview consumes selected columns+bounds.
@dec id=M4-BANK-CONTAIN-001 c=H :: PMOS rows start selected minY+edge margin and advance inward; NMOS rows start maxY-edge margin and advance inward; Nwell spans min edge through last PMOS diffusion+well enclosure+one grid guard; large fixture asserts device bounds+Pdiff enclosure.
@dec id=M4-PLACE-001 c=H :: candidates={topology greedy shared-net/source-drain affinity,diffusion stable S/D+gate signature,congestion high-connectivity spread}; legalize polarity rows serpentine to process sites; reject dropped/duplicate occupancy; score legal HPWL+25*peakBinUtil-0.35*pitch*sharingPairs; physical shapes consume selected coordinates.
@dec id=METAL-AUDIT-001 c=H :: large folded fixture permanently checks zero same-layer cross-net rectangle overlap and zero GEOMETRY.MIN_SPACING diagnostics on metal; dense multicolor top-view crossings may be legal across layers; PHVIEW Show-all/Solo isolates each layer.
@dec id=M4-GRT-001 c=H :: coarse router order=power/global/signal; endpoints=device+external-pin bins; adjacent edges select power/signal layer by capacity,current usage,history,wrong-way penalty; overflow identifies owning nets; only owners ripup; alternate H/V Manhattan each pass; stop zero/stall/max; retain minimum-overflow snapshot+iteration history.
@dec id=M4-WAVE-BUS-001 c=H :: persisted user groups define name+ordered MSB..LSB scalar members+binary/hex radix+collapsed state; sticky label and stable intervals show aggregate cursor/time value; value changes draw crossed-X bus boundaries; simultaneous member events resolve before aggregation; UNKNOWN/CONTENDED/unresolved FLOATING propagate X digits; expand restores scalar lanes without resimulation.
@dec id=M5-TIMING-PHYS-001 c=H :: add physical wire/layer/via capacitance,fanout,switching+critical-path costs to M4 candidates; score order=legal/connectivity,configured timing target,area/congestion/wire/vias,then aspect; critical path may justify larger/less-square winner while noncritical repeats choose smallest well-routed result.
@dec id=M5-INCHSTONES-001 c=H :: order=5.1 routed parasitics+timing physical selection,5.2 fanout graph,5.3 switching activity,5.4 path constraints/slack,5.5 educational dynamic power,5.6 consolidated analysis UI+versioned export; each requires known-answer+hierarchy+determinism+contract+visible UI acceptance.
@dec id=M5-PARASITICS-001 c=H :: Technology physical_parasitics v1 owns default wire fF/um+via fF and optional bounded metalN/viaNN overrides; detailed routes retain layer lengths+via-type counts; missing legacy field receives EDU defaults; coefficients nonnegative finite.
@dec id=M5-PATH-001 c=H :: combinational dependency edge=gate net to each non-rail drain/source net,parallel MOS aggregate per edge; DFS bounded by net count+4096 paths and rejects revisits; paths sort input/output/net IDs; worst-delay tie selects lowest stable index; retain ordered nets+contributing MOS.
@dec id=M5-CONSTRAINT-001 c=H :: Project timingTargetNs optional; None=unconstrained never zero; Some must finite positive and is persisted+undoable+flatten-preserved; every path required=target,slack=target-arrival; critical-path slack is worst due max arrival.
@dec id=M5-CANDIDATE-001 c=H :: time each feasible candidate after full detailed route; rank overflow,detail conflicts,then timing-met; if all violate prefer lower worst delay; unconstrained skips timing; remaining ties=area,wire,vias,placement score,stable candidate ID; publish all summaries in IR/UI.
@dec id=M5-CRITICALITY-001 c=H :: constrained projects derive critical device/net order from baseline routed timing; add legal timing placement clustering path devices and promote nonpower critical nets to priority10 before full global/detail reroute; retain both attempts with floorplan+placement provenance and explicit selected summary ID.
@dec id=M5-ACCEPT-001 c=H :: constrained evaluation routes all topology/diffusion/congestion/timing placements under critical-net priority; acceptance requires selected timingDriven delay strictly below equally legal baselines; identical unconstrained design emits only 3 baselines; flattened hierarchy+JSON restoration must normalize identically.
@dec id=M5-FANOUT-001 c=H :: fanout graph shares flattened simulation connectivity; drivers=explicit input/VDD/GND plus one synthetic CMOS-channel driver per nonrail D/S net; loads=MOS gates+output probes; endpoint UUIDs enable cross-selection; sorted aliases deterministic; waveform groups report sum+max; project persists positive warning threshold, legacy default8.
@dec id=PREVIEW-ACCESS-001 c=H :: fixed terminal remains; renderer preview searches preferred drop layers across complete floorplan width; candidate includes anchor jog+vertical+via stack; first zero cross-net conflict wins, else deterministic minimum; snap guard protects post-grid clearance; exact 4B remains nonzero and needs 2D escape routing.
